# Omni-Changeling's "You may have this creature enter as a copy of any creature on the battlefield, except it has
# changeling" is a replacement effect of its own (CR 614.1c), and CR 614.12 judges which replacement effects apply on the
# permanent as it would exist on the battlefield, "taking into account ... continuous effects that already exist and would
# apply to the permanent". There it is a Saproling (changeling, CR 702.73a), so Life and Limb ("All Forests and all
# Saprolings are 1/1 green Saproling creatures and Forest lands in addition to their other types") makes it a nonbasic
# Forest land, and Blood Moon ("Nonbasic lands are Mountains"), which depends on Life and Limb and applies after it
# (CR 613.8a), makes it a Mountain that has lost the abilities of its rules text (CR 305.7; Blood Moon's ruling: such a land
# does not choose "as" it enters). So Bot1 is not asked to copy the Ornithopter: Omni-Changeling enters as itself, a 1/1
# green Mountain creature land of every creature type (KI-52). The positive control of the copy is
# omni-changeling-convoked-with-three-artifact-creatures-enters-as-a-copy-with-changeling.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Black Lotus
Life and Limb
Blood Moon
Ornithopter
Omni-Changeling
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x20

